      "order": 7,
      "chapterNumber": 7,
      "headline": "Spotting the Tiny Clues Before the Storm",
      "keyInsight": "We usually wait for a loud alarm before fixing our lives. We ignore a sputtering car engine until smoke pours out. We ignore a chilly silence with a partner until someone packs bags. Our brains love grand drama, but reality moves in whispers. A massive career change or relationship breakthrough never starts with a lightning bolt. It starts with a glance, a sigh, or a three-second idea in the shower. When you tune your eyes to tiny moments, you gain a superpower. You see the crack in the foundation before the wall falls down. You catch the seed of a million-dollar project before anyone else notices it.",
